WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:03.325
Most AI hands you an answer.

2
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:06.000
Very little of it shows you why.

3
00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:09.400
Anwar Debes builds the kind that does.

4
00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:16.990
At the University of Agder, he researches Tsetlin Machines:

5
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:23.225
models whose every decision is a set of logical clauses you can read, check, and argue with.

6
00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:30.500
His master's research, glassbox-lm, takes measured steps toward a language model you can read.

7
00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:34.425
Ninety-one hypotheses, written down before the runs.

8
00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:39.325
Every result reported as measured, including the ones that did not work.

9
00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:41.950
He builds AI you can check.

10
00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:48.250
VERITAS proves a guardrail's safety rules, or hands you the exact input that breaks one.

11
00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:54.525
TRACE catches an attack hidden in innocent steps, and signs a ledger anyone can verify.

12
00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:58.850
CANDOR puts a certificate on every answer a network gives.

13
00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:03.202
At NTNU, his bachelor team won the Eureka Prize for

14
00:01:03.212 --> 00:01:08.800
software that finds and removes sensitive content in images and documents.

15
00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:15.275
Today, he is CFO of SafeMediAI, the Norwegian startup behind DeclassifAI.

16
00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:20.240
Outside the lab, he builds game-playing agents, data warehouses,

17
00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:23.175
and apps that run entirely in your browser.

18
00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:28.250
Even his coding agent shows its work: Pixie acts out every step.

19
00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:31.025
One rule runs through all of it.

20
00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:34.650
If a system makes a claim, it should show its work.

21
00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:37.450
Anwar Debes.

